","text":"E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase that catalyzes 'Lys-11'- or 'Lys-33'-linked polyubiquitin chains, with some preference for 'Lys-33' linkages (PubMed:25752577). E3 ubiquitin-protein ligases accept ubiquitin from an E2 ubiquitin-conjugating enzyme in the form of a thioester and then directly transfers the ubiquitin to targeted substrates (PubMed:23479728, PubMed:31578312). Ubiquitinates SEPTIN4, DIABLO/SMAC and HTRA2 in vitro (PubMed:23479728). Modulates pulmonary inflammation by targeting SOCS2 for ubiquitination and subsequent degradation by the proteasome (PubMed:31578312)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}